(label "BUZ_5V" (at 342.9 144.78 180) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify right bottom)) (uuid "e6985964-42e3-5845-8097-0802b469c358"))
(label "BUZ_N" (at 342.9 149.86 180) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify right bottom)) (uuid "4ea06fe9-6c1d-5d2f-8b45-8271335739c2"))
(text "Robot harness. Power path: pack → XT60 → F1 7.5 A → SW1 → INA226 shunt → VBUS (12–16.8 V).\nVBUS → E-stop NC → K1 coil (K1 makes VMOT) → VMOT → board J1 (XT30) and the servo buck.\nVBUS → 5 V buck → Pi (micro-USB pigtail) and board J2. The ESP32 is powered over USB from the Pi.\nCharging: dock pads → SS54 → CC/CV charger → VBUS (charges the pack through the INA226, current reads −).\nDOCK_PAD− goes ONLY to the charger IN−, never to GND: the charger senses current between IN− and OUT−." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 241.3 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left top)) (uuid "74cc579d-19bf-586c-8ef2-fd899a5ece94"))
(text "Wires (02 §1): VBUS/VMOT and pack 18 AWG silicone red/black (tag VMOT); dock pads → charger 18 AWG;\n5 V and 6 V buck outputs 20 AWG; motors 22–24 AWG JST-XH 4p; switches, E-stop NO, DOCK_V 26 AWG JST-XH.\nConnectors: XT60 at the pack, XT30 pigtail to J1, 5.08 screw terminals J2/J3, JST-XH J4–J13 and J16–J19.\nGround rule (02 §3.3): GND_5V and GND_6V run from each buck's OUT− to J2/J3, not back to the pack;\nkeep the J1 GND lead short and thick. GND, GND_5V and GND_6V are one node (inside the bucks and on A1).\nJ8–J13: switch COM → G, contact → S; the 3V3 pin is spare. Home switches use NC (open = home or broken wire).\nPolarity: wire red = +, black = −; meter every lead before the first plug-in (A1 README bring-up)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 264.16 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left top)) (uuid "01e3ad52-25d5-5b46-92ea-583047197303"))
(embedded_fonts no)
)
